    "created_at": "2025-03-12T15:20:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-12T15:20:11Z",
    "body": "Maybe this isn't helpful, but while I was initially convinced by the argument that pushState() is a sort of \"progressive enhancement\", and making it throw would break more things than it'd fix, the more I think about it the more I lean towards the predictability that other browsers have already paved the way towards.\n\nIt'd still be a compat risk for Chrome to match the others here, but hopefully not insurmountable. I think I not-very-strongly lean towards codifying the throwing behavior. Do you have opinions @domenic?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
