    "created_at": "2026-05-19T08:52:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-19T08:52:25Z",
    "body": "We found that throwing, at least for `location`-based navigations, is not web compatible, see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11844#issuecomment-4485908955 , https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11410\n\nChromium still no-ops for `pushState`, while WebKit throws after reaching its limit. Should we switch to not throwing, which seems better in terms of web compat and would be consistent with regular navigations?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
