    "created_at": "2026-05-19T10:26:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-19T13:37:37Z",
    "body": "> Not throwing means you have to check `history.state` after each time you call `pushState()`, right? I think such a change would be acceptable, but it's unfortunate.\n\nIt depends on how it's used. Often it's a progressive enhancement to ensure the app state is reflected in the URL. A common scenario is calling `pushState` on every `mouse` or `input` event resulting on over-syncing.\n\nA no-op here means that the URL would get out of sync in that scenario but at this point this lack of sync is a lesser evil than erroring the whole script.\n\nNote that in that scenario you don't have to constantly check `history.state` as your app can probably function without the URL and internal state staying in sync.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
